#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60d8de59-e926-5de7-b072-2d9bc5fd4392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708950} {:answer/id #uuid "64c2fba2-0c52-5141-9725-6da0b0c8f931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708951} {:answer/id #uuid "79fbb0c1-1d76-5f44-868a-b321ad27dc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708955} {:answer/id #uuid "e7de106c-d9b2-5e94-9144-90e4f8a6532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708966} {:answer/id #uuid "fd72ee49-cd70-55c4-93b4-43f614cbe039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708971}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708950} :answer-field/id #uuid "56fcb1d3-67d6-5ea9-bde4-dbfd2c371945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "be2ee223-c22d-50df-aeba-30822ea412b6" :question/problem "![](images/93/93c6184f39b28a057866bb02e11e5e81a7abea4ff8a9a907670dd30cfc93d557.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,-1)$ to the point $B(1,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,1)$ to the point $O(0,0).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(y)\\mathbf i+(- x - 2 y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-2,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_1$ is supplied, so calculate $C_2$ only. Choose $x=1 - t$ and $y=1 - t$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_2(t)&=(1 - t)\\mathbf i+(1 - t)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(-1)\\mathbf i+(-1)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=1 - t, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=3 t - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_2(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(1 - t)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad+(3 t - 3)(-1) \\\\ &=2 - 2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(2 - 2 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- t^{2} + 2 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=(-2)+(1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082816cd-adb2-5764-b275-537b44ed5d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708973} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3e57d7-6886-5f70-855d-916d50880b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708974} {:answer/id #uuid "500a88a0-b95b-5699-92be-7210c0b44d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708978} {:answer/id #uuid "a60ef435-54a3-5494-aaab-270340def6fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708988} {:answer/id #uuid "aca026b3-f21f-52cb-9c22-cbff1a6e6053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708988} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea7694c9-b91d-5ab8-9575-881b664b850e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c4cbdb7-e069-55a6-9f7a-6aece1f6ad51" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0a4f042748ddadd824bed4ee71bca9724d7ca7dcc376a0ccf7c1353d59ec4fc.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(-2,2)$ to the point $B(-1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(-1,2)$ to the point $D(-1,0).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- x + y)\\mathbf i+(- x - y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=0,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$.\n\nFor $C_1$, use $\\mathbf r_1(t)=(t - 2)\\mathbf i+(2)\\mathbf j$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_2$ is supplied, so calculate $C_1$ only. Choose $x=t - 2$ and $y=2$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_1(t)&=(t - 2)\\mathbf i+(2)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(1)\\mathbf i+(0)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=4 - t, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=- t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(4 - t)(1) \\\\ &\\quad+(- t)(0) \\\\ &=4 - t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(4 - t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- \\frac{t^{2}}{2} + 4 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)+(0)=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192a44ed-bddd-5548-ac6a-d36c1bc38833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708975} {:answer/id #uuid "33546f57-fb12-52b4-8072-63f4dc82e9ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708977} {:answer/id #uuid "dde68bfd-90a8-5a91-8aa2-1b928298d02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708994} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d3de4e-41c8-50b5-9501-1b7d05529664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708995} {:answer/id #uuid "fee2678e-3ab8-5ec6-9837-2ac850156632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708994} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee637fb8-6cdf-504b-b729-4e1e4335ffc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c346b39-a959-52ff-9a46-d063ecc78a01" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e4a78829ce8d1135d46dda1db59c968c0306937d9c5a45b24fa41648a679ea4.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(1,1).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- 2 x - y)\\mathbf i+(- y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=3,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$.\n\nFor $C_1$, use $\\mathbf r_1(t)=(2 t)\\mathbf i+(0)\\mathbf j$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_2$ is supplied, so calculate $C_1$ only. Choose $x=2 t$ and $y=0$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_1(t)&=(2 t)\\mathbf i+(0)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(2)\\mathbf i+(0)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=- 4 t, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(- 4 t)(2) \\\\ &\\quad+(0)(0) \\\\ &=- 8 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(- 8 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- 4 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=(-4)+(3)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f5086d-d269-5b92-ad62-5ad2b3b1fb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708981} {:answer/id #uuid "6a24e281-5ecc-5be7-a701-227a391d4c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708982} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0589a2-9485-547b-9f0e-df2227f06ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708983} {:answer/id #uuid "ca19c7f8-bf15-5f14-9984-f927b1b8011b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708992} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5fd54f-9dd2-5c9b-9920-6709274bb441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708982} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b89f0d4-7500-55ed-b2f9-42ada8a6e5a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d722494c-eec4-5458-86da-556697e8910c" :question/problem "![](images/73/73c6a8268a179f72611fb65e099d1249d48501e4fd4731d03747800e1944fd97.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,2)$ to the point $D(1,3).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- 2 x)\\mathbf i+(x + y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=1,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$.\n\nFor $C_2$, use $\\mathbf r_2(t)=(1)\\mathbf i+(t + 2)\\mathbf j$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_1$ is supplied, so calculate $C_2$ only. Choose $x=1$ and $y=t + 2$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_2(t)&=(1)\\mathbf i+(t + 2)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(0)\\mathbf i+(1)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=-2, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=t + 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_2(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(-2)(0) \\\\ &\\quad+(t + 3)(1) \\\\ &=t + 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(t + 3)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + 3 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=(1)+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59beb523-5acd-535e-ab35-1d78c9002fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708979} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3f5cfd-e8b8-5495-b5c9-4f3d4de1a0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708985} {:answer/id #uuid "85371aec-bdc8-52e1-93c7-e9fe3ac20c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708987} {:answer/id #uuid "a750357d-4248-59ed-9107-c51f460e179a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708989} {:answer/id #uuid "be35a420-e788-5433-9b22-2496a47e8f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708991}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708987} :answer-field/id #uuid "847c158a-9345-5ea7-bf73-6fb6fea0d1bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f80a0398-4595-524e-bcea-5ec5e8f1c913" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0a4f042748ddadd824bed4ee71bca9724d7ca7dcc376a0ccf7c1353d59ec4fc.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(-2,2)$ to the point $B(-1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(-1,2)$ to the point $D(-1,0).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- x - y)\\mathbf i+(2 x)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=- \\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$.\n\nFor $C_2$, use $\\mathbf r_2(t)=(-1)\\mathbf i+(2 - 2 t)\\mathbf j$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_1$ is supplied, so calculate $C_2$ only. Choose $x=-1$ and $y=2 - 2 t$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_2(t)&=(-1)\\mathbf i+(2 - 2 t)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(0)\\mathbf i+(-2)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=2 t - 1, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_2(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(2 t - 1)(0) \\\\ &\\quad+(-2)(-2) \\\\ &=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(4)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[4 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+(4)=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This substitutes $x^2+y$ instead of $x^2-y$." :answer/id #uuid "2b4fe687-b0dc-51d9-92c8-5a2a8ccd3f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(4t^2-5t+3)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709004} {:answer/feedback "This exchanges the roles of $x$ and $y$." :answer/id #uuid "3f9236ca-b7fd-548c-b339-d95303dc6061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(t^2-6t+5)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709006} {:answer/feedback "This drops the initial $x$-coordinate: $x=-1+2t$, not $2t$." :answer/id #uuid "5e504e75-088d-5f98-aa9b-3a9bbab56a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(4t^2+t-2)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709011} {:answer/feedback "The displacement is $(2,-1)$, the speed is $\\sqrt5$, and the substituted function is $4t^2-3t-1$." :answer/id #uuid "7f231255-a4f8-54ac-9ee1-132507005532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(4t^2-3t-1)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709012} {:answer/feedback "The speed is $\\sqrt5$, not $5$." :answer/id #uuid "cb02784f-4be1-5064-8eb1-124276eaeeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\int_0^1(4t^2-3t-1)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709018}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709012} :answer-field/id #uuid "58c21270-aaa8-5bc4-9e88-58d76b7d666c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1911ca35-465b-573d-b9aa-bd829d0d664c" :question/problem "![Segment C from A(-1, 2) to B(1, 1).](images/05/05889a75dfabf783019fb7f4bfc0283999874ade7bd58e564fa6fd153226680d.png)\n\nThe labeled points are the endpoints of the straight segment $C$, traversed from $A$ to $B$. Which definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C (x^2-y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s?\n$$\n\nDo not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a scalar line integral with respect to arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nRead $A=(-1,2)$ and $B=(1,1)$ from the figure. The displacement is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a=(1-(-1))\\mathbf i+(1-2)\\mathbf j=2\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=(-1+2t)\\mathbf i+(2-t)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis starts at $A$ and ends at $B$. Compute the derivative, speed, and substituted function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=2\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{2^2+(-1)^2}=\\sqrt5,\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=(-1+2t)^2-(2-t)\\\\\n&=4t^2-3t-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\int_C(x^2-y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(4t^2-3t-1)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nKeep both the initial coordinates and the signs of the coordinate changes when substituting."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Here $x=2$, $y=2t$, and $\\mathrm{d}s=2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." :answer/id #uuid "4ec0d50b-82bb-509f-b971-603150cc6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_0^1(2+\\sin(2t))\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709009} {:answer/feedback "The substitution is correct, but the arc-length factor is missing." :answer/id #uuid "c2ed4e86-6684-5045-81fa-61e2c3640669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_0^1(2+\\sin(2t))\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709016} {:answer/feedback "The coordinate $y=2t$ must also be substituted inside the sine." :answer/id #uuid "c5e916b9-3e70-5799-81b6-ba0de7e71a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_0^1(2+\\sin t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709017} {:answer/feedback "The speed is $2$, not its square $4$." :answer/id #uuid "db407ba6-9429-5cf2-8d14-d4eab776211c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_0^1(2+\\sin(2t))\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709019} {:answer/feedback "The coordinate $x$ stays at $2$; it does not equal $2t$." :answer/id #uuid "dd75064e-7740-5fb9-adf9-d37126b0ced4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_0^1(2t+\\sin(2t))\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709020}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709009} :answer-field/id #uuid "89227660-85b8-50ae-a4fa-42b4ee21bb19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a47b540-8cfb-5384-a564-563e618fd5cf" :question/problem "Which definite integral is equivalent to the line integral of $f(x,y)=x+\\sin y$ along the line segment from $(2,0)$ to $(2,2)$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a scalar line integral with respect to arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe endpoint position vectors are $\\mathbf a=2\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf b=2\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j$. Parameterize the segment by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf i+2t\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ we obtain the stated endpoints. Along the segment, $x=2$ and $y=2t$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=2\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{0^2+2^2}=2,\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=2+\\sin(2t).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitution gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C (x+\\sin y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=2\\int_0^1 (2+\\sin(2t))\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe factor $2$ comes from arc length, not from the function substitution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The supplied parameterization reaches $A$ at $u=2$. The interval $[0,1]$ covers only half the segment." :answer/id #uuid "0f182bf6-85d6-53b9-a9f0-c6df9a99f86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2\\int_0^1(u^2-7u+8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709001} {:answer/feedback "The arc-length factor $\\sqrt2$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "2776e15a-a183-539e-9cf5-0a56c678e970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_0^2(u^2-7u+8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709003} {:answer/feedback "The interval is $[0,2]$, the speed is $\\sqrt2$, and scalar arc-length integration is unchanged by reversal." :answer/id #uuid "45a5dd90-3c9f-5f42-9bf3-a8b1abebee38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2\\int_0^2(u^2-7u+8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709007} {:answer/feedback "Substitute $x=3-u$ and $y=1+u$ into $x^2-y$." :answer/id #uuid "4ce195d0-ea3d-5b44-b982-99d66e2cb81f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2\\int_0^2(u^2+u+2)\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709008} {:answer/feedback "Reversing traversal does not negate an integral with respect to arc length; the speed remains positive." :answer/id #uuid "a145f1c9-60f5-51d6-8a16-be85a22b1a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt2\\int_0^2(u^2-7u+8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709007} :answer-field/id #uuid "a64a7a88-c22e-55be-ba69-3fe437e0ce77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e062a161-c337-50a1-afc4-d82a8fde42a5" :question/problem "![Segment C from A(1, 3) to B(3, 1).](images/fe/fe2d9715d2f7e62e684d1a4326c7ebe1a3d052e161bdb3de061cdf5fb6640fed.png)\n\nLet $C$ be the straight segment from $A$ to $B$ shown above, and let $f(x,y)=x^2-y$. Use the parameterization\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u)=(3-u)\\mathbf i+(1+u)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nWhich definite integral, with increasing limits and parameter $u$, is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Determine the parameter interval from the endpoints. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The figure gives $A=(1,3)$ and $B=(3,1)$. Locate these points in the supplied parameterization:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(0)=3\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j=\\mathbf b,\\qquad\n\\mathbf r(2)=\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf j=\\mathbf a.\n$$\n\nThus $0\\le u\\le2$ traces the same segment once, from $B$ to $A$. A scalar line integral with respect to arc length does not change when the traversal is reversed. We may therefore use these increasing limits for $C$.\n\nDifferentiate and substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(u)&=-\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(u)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+1^2}=\\sqrt2,\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(u))&=(3-u)^2-(1+u)\\\\\n&=u^2-7u+8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe arc-length factor is the positive speed, even though $x$ decreases. Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n&=\\int_0^2 f(\\mathbf r(u))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(u)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\\\\n&=\\sqrt2\\int_0^2(u^2-7u+8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe usual interval $[0,1]$ belongs to the endpoint parameterization $\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)$; it cannot be attached unchanged to this different parameterization."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709558 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This alternative uses freeze-x." :answer/id #uuid "27ba9dfe-f64e-5512-a689-4837086c74b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{- t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709559} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: square; freeze-y." :answer/id #uuid "2bbd5ea4-e682-5f23-b848-ea29056db2de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709560} {:answer/feedback "Use both coordinate substitutions, the positive speed, and the parameter interval." :answer/id #uuid "db8b37a1-e144-5988-afb1-eb1c64ee217c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{0}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709585} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: square; correct coordinate substitution." :answer/id #uuid "deed7f79-7535-5057-9891-8ce69946278a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{0}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709586} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: square; freeze-x." :answer/id #uuid "f7e53970-4000-55d9-864c-17e82b66256d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{- t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709591}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709585} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1391d30-dbcb-596f-93eb-668af2bd594c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "277d11dd-464a-54d1-8402-9956f8889323" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the straight segment from $A=(0,0)$ to $B=(1,-1)$. Let $f(x,y)=e^{x+y}$. Which definite integral is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The endpoint position vectors give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=\\langle t,- t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ this gives $A=(0,0)$ and $B=(1,-1)$, respectively.\n\nDifferentiate, compute the speed, and substitute both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 1,-1\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(1)^2+(-1)^2}=\\sqrt{2},\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=e^{(t)+(- t)}\\\\\n&=e^{0}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the scalar arc-length formula,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{1}f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t,\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(e^{0}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: orientation; freeze-x." :answer/id #uuid "2c30f74b-fe8f-5838-aa6c-7a6e2d4739e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(-2+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709561} {:answer/feedback "Use both coordinate substitutions, the positive speed, and the parameter interval." :answer/id #uuid "63a086ea-8d21-5b69-b6a1-157d11789656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t - 2+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709569} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses drop-x-offset." :answer/id #uuid "7529e0b3-f6c9-565e-a665-8416ce5b3cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709576} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: orientation; drop-x-offset." :answer/id #uuid "a3ced842-a362-5625-ae57-7e937476f2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709579} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: orientation; correct coordinate substitution." :answer/id #uuid "baa745d9-d7ba-59c1-b701-51eae388acdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t - 2+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709569} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4b9c34-12a5-599f-ad46-dc5d18d7b8be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "51ed470e-e860-5168-9b27-f039ebc84626" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the straight segment from $A=(-2,2)$ to $B=(-4,2)$. Let $f(x,y)=x+\\sin y$. Which definite integral is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The endpoint position vectors give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=\\langle - 2 t - 2,2\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ this gives $A=(-2,2)$ and $B=(-4,2)$, respectively.\n\nDifferentiate, compute the speed, and substitute both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle -2,0\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+(0)^2}=2,\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=(- 2 t - 2)+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 t - 2+\\sin\\left(2\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the scalar arc-length formula,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{1}f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t,\\\\\n&=2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t - 2+\\sin\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This alternative uses reverse-y-rate." :answer/id #uuid "34bcaae7-69a2-51e9-9a30-c3d508e549e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t^{2} + 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709562} {:answer/feedback "Use both coordinate substitutions, the positive speed, and the parameter interval." :answer/id #uuid "5a70df67-3bbf-5374-b13e-3cc64000df8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t^{2} - 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709568} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses freeze-x." :answer/id #uuid "d2cc4dff-9f93-5342-8221-22a71c5ab977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709584} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: missing; reverse-y-rate." :answer/id #uuid "ed1e3846-938d-5cee-bf4a-48f5f3daa150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t^{2} + 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709589} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: missing; correct coordinate substitution." :answer/id #uuid "f7bf4ecb-cb23-5bff-9eab-6c3baf7fb3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t^{2} - 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709590}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709568} :answer-field/id #uuid "3badadb9-107a-57d9-ba91-313bf8b8aca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6e17bc03-2612-5130-b849-8dad2b9e95ed" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the straight segment from $A=(0,0)$ to $B=(2,2)$. Let $f(x,y)=x^2-y$. Which definite integral is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The endpoint position vectors give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=\\langle 2 t,2 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ this gives $A=(0,0)$ and $B=(2,2)$, respectively.\n\nDifferentiate, compute the speed, and substitute both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 2,2\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(2)^2+(2)^2}=2 \\sqrt{2},\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=(2 t)^2-(2 t)\\\\\n&=4 t^{2} - 2 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the scalar arc-length formula,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{1}f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t,\\\\\n&=2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t^{2} - 2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: manhattan; reverse-x-rate." :answer/id #uuid "529a775e-3f6a-58a4-832f-9c50eaf7d618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709567} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: manhattan; freeze-y." :answer/id #uuid "7407a1b0-20ff-5c5c-9848-676b8bb8cb6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709574} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: manhattan; correct coordinate substitution." :answer/id #uuid "a0fe690c-6e28-51cd-95f3-7b0ec11d0843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709578} {:answer/feedback "Use both coordinate substitutions, the positive speed, and the parameter interval." :answer/id #uuid "bcebd75b-b713-5d09-9bb1-c5dcafee2d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709582} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses freeze-y." :answer/id #uuid "ca1243fc-20c5-50af-aa03-d73e167f4aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709583}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709582} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6b2a9d-840b-5b3d-94b3-e958332b0dc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "706e2cab-09a9-596b-bbb2-24fb6bfeb7f5" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the straight segment from $A=(0,0)$ to $B=(2,-2)$. Let $f(x,y)=2x+y$. Which definite integral is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The endpoint position vectors give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=\\langle 2 t,- 2 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ this gives $A=(0,0)$ and $B=(2,-2)$, respectively.\n\nDifferentiate, compute the speed, and substitute both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 2,-2\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(2)^2+(-2)^2}=2 \\sqrt{2},\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=2(2 t)+(- 2 t)\\\\\n&=2 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the scalar arc-length formula,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{1}f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t,\\\\\n&=2 \\sqrt{2}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: orientation; correct coordinate substitution." :answer/id #uuid "64f28324-3f27-5137-acd3-6dd7f6cbecab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709570} {:answer/feedback "Use both coordinate substitutions, the positive speed, and the parameter interval." :answer/id #uuid "68d1c007-4384-5d7f-bd1c-83316e5f12ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709571} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses endpoint-y-rate." :answer/id #uuid "7454389f-c2eb-5bfc-b8e4-bc3b3eb03a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709575} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses wrong speed: orientation; drop-y-offset." :answer/id #uuid "7e400d01-f17e-5a67-acf6-6f007d53373a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709577} {:answer/feedback "This alternative uses drop-y-offset." :answer/id #uuid "b8085ea5-ce02-5b94-a912-9eb3c94107fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709580}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709571} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5ef9a1-6087-522f-952c-fdd10ab4d6fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e55a0a5d-0568-5149-8095-465b8fd9d633" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the straight segment from $A=(-1,-1)$ to $B=(-1,-2)$. Let $f(x,y)=1+x-\\cos y$. Which definite integral is equivalent to $\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The endpoint position vectors give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(t)&=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)\\\\\n&=\\langle -1,- t - 1\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ and $t=1$ this gives $A=(-1,-1)$ and $B=(-1,-2)$, respectively.\n\nDifferentiate, compute the speed, and substitute both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 0,-1\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(0)^2+(-1)^2}=1,\\\\\nf(\\mathbf r(t))&=1+(-1)-\\cos\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\\\\n&=0-\\cos\\left(- t - 1\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the scalar arc-length formula,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{1}f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t,\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(0-\\cos\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52343ada-5af0-598f-8b5a-bdccbefa1592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{6}{t - 6}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709832} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbb3277-aaf7-562d-a425-ceb7b1b0aa8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709835} {:answer/id #uuid "9c596b86-f808-564a-bdc5-d0e1a5b3056a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2}{t - 6}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709840} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff2d983-5668-5086-bc20-f63dd86474fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{8}{t - 6}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709841} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a8a869-358c-50a9-bc25-41aa8db843d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{4 \\left(2 - t\\right)}{t - 6}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709841} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21eb1f9-9399-5a8a-8853-0744af486cbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a206610-d806-590d-aa77-0f20c2968e64" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ traversed along the line segment from $(-6,2,6)$ to $(-5,4,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(t - 6,2 t + 2,6 - 2 t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(-6,2,6\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(-5,4,4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(1,2,-2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(1)^2+(2)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\  &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\frac{(2 t + 2)+(6 - 2 t)}{t - 6} \\\\  &=\\frac{8}{t - 6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{8}{t - 6}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1800ff2c-730f-56ae-a3eb-584c6ad28d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t - 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709824} {:answer/id #uuid "3cfc6a39-6e6d-53db-bbe1-0976c184af42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)}{t - 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709831} {:answer/id #uuid "704cf6f6-bd41-5f3a-a0e6-8512f06cd99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2}{t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709839} {:answer/id #uuid "b5389089-4a4a-52dd-aff1-0710abe89e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{4}{t - 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709845} {:answer/id #uuid "f51e9756-2de6-5313-b25c-e87f59d9c849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(2 t - 1\\right)}{t - 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709824} :answer-field/id #uuid "39bfebeb-dc86-57f1-9c8e-ed757957e165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7033c3e6-52f7-555b-932a-a2536dae6dba" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ traversed along the line segment from $(4,-2,4)$ to $(3,0,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(4 - t,2 t - 2,4 - 2 t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(4,-2,4\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(3,0,2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-1,2,-2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(2)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\  &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\frac{(2 t - 2)+(4 - 2 t)}{4 - t} \\\\  &=- \\frac{2}{t - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t - 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04915040-4120-56d3-8085-1365fa484837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6 t + 2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709820} {:answer/id #uuid "0f90488b-431d-5aa1-9402-75724da4ba19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6 t - 2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709822} {:answer/id #uuid "39e00f42-91cb-5325-87ca-c8afbbce9328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4 t - 2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709828} {:answer/id #uuid "5957f581-365d-5440-99ef-faa86cee96ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709833} {:answer/id #uuid "6e01469e-eebc-570e-9636-b6d5283a4b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2 t - 2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709837}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709822} :answer-field/id #uuid "acb10bdd-7966-57f7-99ce-bef8c376b3f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c88a3331-2350-5539-a63d-23fa856f75ca" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x, y, z) = x + y + z$, traversed along the line segment from $(-4, 2, 0)$ to $(-2, 3, 3)$?" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(2 t - 4,t + 2,3 t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(-4,2,0\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(-2,3,3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(2,1,3\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(2)^2+(1)^2+(3)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(2 t - 4)+(t + 2)+(3 t) \\\\  &=6 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6 t - 2)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd2b01b-e130-53ae-a50e-3286b57ba825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{8}{2 t - 5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709830} {:answe