(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(2)^2+(-2)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  &=2 \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\frac{(2 - 2 t)+(2 t + 6)}{2 t - 5} \\\\  &=\\frac{8}{2 t - 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=2 \\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{8}{2 t - 5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f859f6e-be3d-50a6-a69d-e761dbebc35a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(t - 1\\right)}{t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709821} {:answer/id #uuid "1309330d-8f54-5b11-bac8-ceb1317a5dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(- t - 1\\right)}{t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709823} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d1ca4-1850-50cc-98b0-d61feb454657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{5}{t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709834} {:answer/id #uuid "a041c66f-82e1-579d-8198-9de7ffb7d508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709842} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5942e5-846f-52c2-ba11-ce71de45c477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709846}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709842} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b1d16c-215a-568e-8043-657baed82f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f191647d-a4c4-5898-a780-f5d324565917" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ traversed along the line segment from $(2,-3,5)$ to $(1,-1,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(2 - t,2 t - 3,5 - 2 t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(2,-3,5\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(1,-1,3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-1,2,-2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(2)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\  &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\frac{(2 t - 3)+(5 - 2 t)}{2 - t} \\\\  &=- \\frac{2}{t - 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04aaf0b0-fed4-5e9b-9819-b1e4800a1458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{229 \\sqrt{14}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709868} {:answer/id #uuid "0d4b7065-5325-5be5-9249-b00a0a3d5117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{148 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709869} {:answer/id #uuid "acd07dfb-a10a-52fc-9db5-9f18010c65b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709886} {:answer/id #uuid "c68e8a9d-2f42-5d22-a0ac-83bf70f6bcaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{229 \\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709889} {:answer/id #uuid "fb30e371-d760-54a6-ac57-9fb447397d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{229 \\sqrt{13}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709894}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709868} :answer-field/id #uuid "2267c501-85d5-5df8-825f-7221334904bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "33123352-d1fb-5568-bf8e-4e47c856da58" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(4,4,3)$ to $(2,3,6).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(4 - 2 t,4 - t,3 t + 3\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(4,4,3\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(2,3,6\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-2,-1,3\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+(-1)^2+(3)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(4 - 2 t)(4 - t)^2 \\\\  &=- 2 t^{3} + 20 t^{2} - 64 t + 64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the expanded polynomial and subtract the endpoint values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(- 2 t^{3} + 20 t^{2} - 64 t + 64)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\left[- \\frac{t^{4}}{2} + \\frac{20 t^{3}}{3} - 32 t^{2} + 64 t\\right]_0^1 \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\left(\\left(\\frac{229}{6}\\right)-(0)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{229 \\sqrt{14}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17c5d785-ca51-5f28-b10b-d5cd1971bdba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{61 \\sqrt{6}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709870} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbaad3a-0ace-512c-afec-7b5f3d646de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{45 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709875} {:answer/id #uuid "e065f84a-60c8-5246-a06f-da5106fe2633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{26 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709890} {:answer/id #uuid "f24b3a82-2314-5e56-bda7-cb5e2d1fa444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{61 \\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709893} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4bb074-3d9c-58e2-bdc5-4a3f5cffddb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{61 \\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709895}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709870} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc093f11-1f20-5db9-b82b-e2aeaf12b8a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709887}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "412d2f50-93cf-50c4-894d-282b66d2f931" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(2,3,-1)$ to $(3,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(t + 2,3 - 2 t,t - 1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(2,3,-1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(3,1,0\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(1,-2,1\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(1)^2+(-2)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(t + 2)(3 - 2 t)^2 \\\\  &=4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2} - 15 t + 18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the expanded polynomial and subtract the endpoint values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2} - 15 t + 18)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\left[t^{4} - \\frac{4 t^{3}}{3} - \\frac{15 t^{2}}{2} + 18 t\\right]_0^1 \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\left(\\left(\\frac{61}{6}\\right)-(0)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{61 \\sqrt{6}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b51f67-618a-5cbc-9446-f7a943947407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{65 \\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709880} {:answer/id #uuid "7764e321-87b0-50ac-8937-e9d98878ace7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "19 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709881} {:answer/id #uuid "96b7d958-f38c-5263-bce4-dddde3ae6fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{65 \\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709884} {:answer/id #uuid "9df8b7d4-2e88-5bfa-ad1a-68e55f0a58f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{65 \\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709885} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5ddfc3-6004-50c9-b2d0-65ce2e903656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{45 \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709892}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709884} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ebd4fdb-8eae-5097-8899-d87185517aa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "41ccb218-51e7-515a-b64b-9ff991662da4" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(3,3,2)$ to $(2,2,4).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(3 - t,3 - t,2 t + 2\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(3,3,2\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(2,2,4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-1,-1,2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-1)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(3 - t)(3 - t)^2 \\\\  &=- t^{3} + 9 t^{2} - 27 t + 27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the expanded polynomial and subtract the endpoint values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(- t^{3} + 9 t^{2} - 27 t + 27)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\left[- \\frac{t^{4}}{4} + 3 t^{3} - \\frac{27 t^{2}}{2} + 27 t\\right]_0^1 \\\\  &=\\sqrt{6}\\left(\\left(\\frac{65}{4}\\right)-(0)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{65 \\sqrt{6}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce98cae-13e7-5cc7-b70b-92268d666b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{76 \\sqrt{10}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709871} {:answer/id #uuid "27c5d55f-3adb-57ea-b603-099f209558d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709873} {:answer/id #uuid "363eac8b-7b87-5441-8b3e-47d657750fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{175 \\sqrt{10}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709877} {:answer/id #uuid "908b32bf-9f4b-51da-afb3-efd1b0084c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{175 \\sqrt{13}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709882} {:answer/id #uuid "c314b6a6-9721-5d26-9bbe-d9b8b569574d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{175 \\sqrt{14}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709888} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e54cb4-1b83-50e4-956e-4a1d34406ad6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eae8aefe-d7fa-5f8a-aaf8-170237bb2dfb" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(4,2,2)$ to $(1,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(4 - 3 t,t + 2,2 - 2 t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(4,2,2\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(1,3,0\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-3,1,-2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-3)^2+(1)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(4 - 3 t)(t + 2)^2 \\\\  &=- 3 t^{3} - 8 t^{2} + 4 t + 16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the expanded polynomial and subtract the endpoint values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(- 3 t^{3} - 8 t^{2} + 4 t + 16)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\left[- \\frac{3 t^{4}}{4} - \\frac{8 t^{3}}{3} + 2 t^{2} + 16 t\\right]_0^1 \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\left(\\left(\\frac{175}{12}\\right)-(0)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{175 \\sqrt{14}}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c3da79d-ebb2-5e99-8771-89b84bb9d048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709897} {:answer/id #uuid "48feb464-f6de-5ff9-8070-a789ae952e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709900} {:answer/id #uuid "6151ba92-2d71-5adb-90c7-3db071fda483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{18 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709901} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdcf3f3-b29b-53c6-b5a0-8785e288c1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(2 - \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709903} {:answer/id #uuid "e83340aa-9966-58b1-9ad8-b5c416594c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(2 - \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709916}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709897} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23e5cae-7780-5b6b-ae9f-52dc1dffcdc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "65076c36-16b6-5b2b-890e-1f4a785e7c2b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}(x+z))\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(-2,4,-4)$ to $(-3,6,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(- t - 2,2 t + 4,2 t - 4\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(-2,4,-4\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(-3,6,-2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-1,2,2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(2)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}((- t - 2)+(2 t - 4))\\right) \\\\  &=\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $u=\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $\\mathrm{d}u=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The new bounds are $u(0)=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $u(1)=- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\int_{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}}\\cos u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left[\\sin u\\right]_{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}} \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left(\\sin\\left(- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}\\right)-\\sin\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-(1)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{6 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220e937c-d0bc-564c-92e0-d31478cbb16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(e + e^{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709896} {:answer/id #uuid "82fc3e54-c3e3-5880-a956-69c9041c4f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21} \\left(- e + e^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709904} {:answer/id #uuid "89889665-caf4-53e1-ab78-55050af287b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21} \\left(- e + e^{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709905} {:answer/id #uuid "8fc118df-6cb2-598d-a1b3-a0e26051d3d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5} e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709906} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b39235-f47d-5717-87f1-91049a8c6587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(- e + e^{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709905} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6dc66b6-544a-5aaa-9133-5e3a99c24acb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d83dd492-f46e-5853-aca9-edea015fd94e" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{e}^{yz}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(3,1,1)$ to $(7,3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(4 t + 3,2 t + 1,t + 1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(3,1,1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(7,3,2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(4,2,1\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(4)^2+(2)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(4 t + 3)e^{(2 t + 1)(t + 1)} \\\\  &=\\left(4 t + 3\\right) e^{2 t^{2} + 3 t + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{21}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\left(4 t + 3\\right) e^{2 t^{2} + 3 t + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $u=2 t^{2} + 3 t + 1$ and $\\mathrm{d}u=(4 t + 3)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The new bounds are $u(0)=1$ and $u(1)=6$. Since $x(t)=1\\,u^{\\prime}(t)$, the differential contributes the factor $1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\sqrt{21}\\int_{1}^{6}e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &=\\sqrt{21}\\left[e^u\\right]_{1}^{6} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{21}\\left(e^{6}-e^{1}\\right) \\\\  &=\\sqrt{21}\\left(e^{6}-(e)\\right) \\\\  &=\\sqrt{21} \\left(- e + e^{6}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e3408f-de20-5473-87d8-37494bcd3714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{17} \\left(-1 + e^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709898} {:answer/id #uuid "46bfacca-6623-5ede-be4e-94d34f49124d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{69} \\left(-1 + e^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709899} {:answer/id #uuid "90f19e6e-fef8-5953-b593-62658202fdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{69} e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709907} {:answer/id #uuid "bba69791-33f4-51e2-8cac-99336fa9355d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{69} \\left(1 + e^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709910} {:answer/id #uuid "e04e2fc3-6107-5f09-9454-7322ca033948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{69} \\left(-1 + e^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709915}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709915} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdef24c2-fca6-55d3-9796-e7d748662aaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "df19524c-8794-5097-aa7f-03dc942c6b98" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{e}^{yz}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(0,0,0)$ to $(-8,-2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(- 8 t,- 2 t,- t\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(0,0,0\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(-8,-2,-1\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-8,-2,-1\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-8)^2+(-2)^2+(-1)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{69}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(- 8 t)e^{(- 2 t)(- t)} \\\\  &=- 8 t e^{2 t^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{69}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(- 8 t e^{2 t^{2}})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $u=2 t^{2}$ and $\\mathrm{d}u=(4 t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The new bounds are $u(0)=0$ and $u(1)=2$. Since $x(t)=-2\\,u^{\\prime}(t)$, the differential contributes the factor $-2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=- 2 \\sqrt{69}\\int_{0}^{2}e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &=- 2 \\sqrt{69}\\left[e^u\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\  &=- 2 \\sqrt{69}\\left(e^{2}-e^{0}\\right) \\\\  &=- 2 \\sqrt{69}\\left(e^{2}-(1)\\right) \\\\  &=- 2 \\sqrt{69} \\left(-1 + e^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715104 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1651a2b6-adec-51c6-98be-91f7069d26fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715108} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8267f8-9df6-5a66-956d-3004bef9599c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715111} {:answer/id #uuid "58393c80-720a-521c-adc7-ac65dbbded12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715114} {:answer/id #uuid "817be77c-1959-505d-9d41-7b5dcb888086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715123} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bd02c6-d5db-5488-a294-6e77b74e0622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{8},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715108} :answer-field/id #uuid "0491cbeb-7434-5942-ba96-f39d523106f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06cde7b6-bdbd-5aad-9bad-8fe8e922719e" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} - 3 x + 2 \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=4 x - 3 \\\\ f_{y}&=4 y + 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4 x - 3&=0 \\\\ 4 y + 12&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x,\\ v=y + 3$. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 u&=3 \\\\ u&=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ v&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Recover the original coordinates using $x=u,\\ y=v - 3$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(\\frac{3}{4},-3)$. Each satisfies every component equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1294ff4d-7424-56e3-9266-d82312ad0d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715107} {:answer/id #uuid "596f400c-f861-5094-8681-30e0f831dc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715115} {:answer/id #uuid "8d76c37e-ccb8-54fd-af34-072a93a1a46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715125} {:answer/id #uuid "ac346812-9f90-5aed-849f-fd7d1fca1f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715127} {:answer/id #uuid "ed507749-492b-5106-944b-d1bafc39b059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,- \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715144}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715115} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfa9fa01-6bad-5728-b9fb-4ee10e7cd735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0fb0c4c3-aaf7-5de8-a684-b70eb6e5f681" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=2 \\left(y + 1\\right)^{2} + \\ln{\\left(\\left(x + 2\\right)^{2} + 2 \\right)}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=\\frac{2 \\left(x + 2\\right)}{\\left(x + 2\\right)^{2} + 2} \\\\ f_{y}&=4 y + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2 \\left(x + 2\\right)}{\\left(x + 2\\right)^{2} + 2}&=0 \\\\ 4 y + 4&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x + 2,\\ v=y + 1$. Since $u^2+2>0$, the first component vanishes exactly when $u=0$. The other equation gives $v=0$. Recover the original coordinates using $x=u - 2,\\ y=v - 1$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(-2,-1)$. Each satisfies every component equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02137bb5-f64e-5275-9b8c-0fb3fea4ed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(\\frac{1}{2},1)$ and $(\\frac{3}{2},1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715101} {:answer/id #uuid "294a159f-f169-53c4-a0bd-375de1afd8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(-1,1)$ and $(-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715110} {:answer/id #uuid "39e26a8d-87e1-59db-bae9-3fd0214da726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,0)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715112} {:answer/id #uuid "aec1405a-9cc3-51ca-9e8d-22af79c19a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(3,1)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715128} {:answer/id #uuid "cc34d80c-078d-5175-8c64-be2e3dff4e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(-3,1)$ and $(-5,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715128} :answer-field/id #uuid "04826389-8c8e-5cda-a17d-2ccb2792101b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1767b5a-8ec1-55b1-bff0-d7872bb7d1d3" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=\\left(\\left(x - 3\\right)^{2} - \\left(y - 1\\right)^{2}\\right) e^{x - 3}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=\\left(2 x + \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2} - \\left(y - 1\\right)^{2} - 6\\right) e^{x - 3} \\\\ f_{y}&=- 2 \\left(y - 1\\right) e^{x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\left(2 x + \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2} - \\left(y - 1\\right)^{2} - 6\\right) e^{x - 3}&=0 \\\\ - 2 \\left(y - 1\\right) e^{x - 3}&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x - 3,\\ v=y - 1$. Since $e^{u}>0$, divide both equations by this factor. The second equation gives $v=0$. Substitution into the first gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u \\left(u + 2\\right)&=0 \\\\ u&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad u=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep both factors; dividing by $u$ would lose a point. Recover the original coordinates using $x=u + 3,\\ y=v + 1$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(3,1)$ and $(1,1)$. Each satisfies every component equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "644e4b10-aa0d-509e-9522-6c15a9549643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715119} {:answer/id #uuid "c454c618-c990-51b6-889b-c9f8bd028da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715135} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a5cb928-145d-5e0f-8516-5ffcad213a6f" :answer-field/key "$(-4,-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0b76aa5-0889-56b9-b999-cd3e4ea8ac7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715132} {:answer/id #uuid "edb1f167-b117-516d-ad25-ece3a4cb8095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715145}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715132} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e8d9a70-077f-5e00-a026-d24084750077" :answer-field/key "$(-4,-7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c0c1516-8f65-579a-8f66-b561df477c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715116} {:answer/id #uuid "c2957c3f-8350-54fe-a949-c5b3e86ca563" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715134}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715134} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f18782-f2da-5412-92e1-d91efde691db" :answer-field/key "$(-8,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a8a74fa-00cf-5ca1-86de-80f80275fa92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715122} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc3b2b8-e987-557c-8d44-e518884a31fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715122} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb4e5873-bbdd-589b-84d3-a4d4700844a0" :answer-field/key "$(-4,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c470fc31-614a-5b25-ad2c-05caa5659261" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=x + 2 + \\frac{8}{y - 3} - \\frac{y - 3}{x + 2}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$. The domain is $x\\ne -2,\\ y\\ne 3$.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=1 + \\frac{y - 3}{\\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}} \\\\ f_{y}&=- \\frac{8}{\\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{1}{x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1 + \\frac{y - 3}{\\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}}&=0 \\\\ - \\frac{8}{\\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{1}{x + 2}&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x + 2,\\ v=y - 3$. The first equation gives $v=-u^2/1$. Because $u,v\\ne0$, substitution in the second and multiplication by $u^4$ are valid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8+u^{3}&=0 \\\\ u^3&=-8 \\\\ u&=-2 \\\\ v&=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Recover the original coordinates using $x=u - 2,\\ y=v + 3$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(-4,-1)$. Each satisfies every component equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b51f4e8-0208-5589-ae97-68b24880e5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715105} {:answer/id #uuid "be5c4c4b-9920-5c8a-b25e-ca791a89fc66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715105} :answer-field/id #uuid "61e796bc-5bfd-5b3d-b899-1f85d81ad269" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7cfd159-c822-58a1-903f-d9344c393aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715130} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c4a391-25eb-5377-beca-92dbf0fa15a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715146} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab5448c-d512-577b-b862-912774ca49b7" :answer-field/key "$(1,\\frac{\\pi}{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "780853e5-5c89-53bb-b875-4478a2919983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715120} {:answer/id #uuid "780e51d1-2809-5942-87eb-11a1ae7561f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715121}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715121} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb362292-7e7e-58c8-bcb7-d00b8a126ecd" :answer-field/key "$(1,\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2489a509-d793-51cc-ba69-b9d03f48e8fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715109} {:answer/id #uuid "d6354534-59f2-5ab8-b37d-ccfd6aac6ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715141}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715109} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdbb9ce6-e15e-5147-8501-ab6059416297" :answer-field/key "$(2,\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e50aa7db-2d04-5790-8062-ba00a39f59e9" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2} - 2 \\left(x - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(2 y - 6 \\right)}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$. The domain is $3\\le y<\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 3$.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=2 x - 2 \\cos{\\left(2 y - 6 \\right)} - 2 \\\\ f_{y}&=4 \\left(x - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(2 y - 6 \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 x - 2 \\cos{\\left(2 y - 6 \\right)} - 2&=0 \\\\ 4 \\left(x - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(2 y - 6 \\right)}&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x - 1,\\ v=y - 3$. The first equation gives $u=\\cos{\\left(2 v \\right)}$. After substitution and division by the nonzero constant $4$, the second equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin{\\left(2 v \\right)} \\cos{\\left(2 v \\right)}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA product is zero if at least one factor is zero. In $0\\le 2 v<\\pi$, this gives $v=0$ or $v=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. The corresponding values of $u$ are $1$ and $0$, respectively. The upper boundary is excluded. Recover the original coordinates using $x=u + 1,\\ y=v + 3$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(2,3)$ and $(1,\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 3)$. Each satisfies every component equation."}]}
